From aa0900f7bc378566324ccf34b8a89f225b9fe991 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:58:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dx-rt: do not fetch build dependencies during do_install
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

do_install runs `pip install .` with --no-deps, which suppresses runtime
dependency resolution but not BUILD dependency resolution. Without
--no-build-isolation, pip creates a fresh build venv and downloads
setuptools/wheel from PyPI to populate it:

    Failed to establish a new connection: [Errno -5] No address associated
      with hostname
    ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement
      setuptools>=40.8.0 (from versions: none)
    ERROR: Failed to build '.../python_package' when installing build
      dependencies

BitBake grants network access only to do_fetch; do_install has none on a
correctly isolated builder, so this fails anywhere the build host cannot
reach PyPI from a build task. Recipes must not fetch outside do_fetch.

Add --no-build-isolation so pip uses the build backend already staged in the
native sysroot, and add python3-setuptools-native to DEPENDS so it is
actually there — without it, disabling isolation moves the failure from
'cannot download setuptools' to 'cannot find setuptools'.

Note: PIP_NO_BUILD_ISOLATION in the task environment is NOT a reliable
substitute; it was confirmed exported into the do_install script and pip
still took the isolation path.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5[1m]
---
 recipes-runtime/dx-rt/dx-rt_3.4.1.bb | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/recipes-runtime/dx-rt/dx-rt_3.4.1.bb b/recipes-runtime/dx-rt/dx-rt_3.4.1.bb
index adb9cb2..3a3ff08 100644
--- a/recipes-runtime/dx-rt/dx-rt_3.4.1.bb
+++ b/recipes-runtime/dx-rt/dx-rt_3.4.1.bb
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ INITSCRIPT_PARAMS = "defaults 90"
 DEPENDS += "libonnxruntime"
 DEPENDS += "python3 python3-pybind11"
 DEPENDS += "python3-native chrpath-native"
-DEPENDS += "python3-pip-native python3-wheel-native"
+DEPENDS += "python3-pip-native python3-wheel-native python3-setuptools-native"
 
 # ------------------------------------------------------------------
 # CMake feature toggles to avoid configure failure:
@@ -145,6 +145,7 @@ do_install:append() {
     cd ${S}/python_package
     python3 -m pip install . \
         --no-deps \
+        --no-build-isolation \
         --no-cache-dir \
         --target="${D}${PYTHON_SITEPACKAGES_DIR}"
 
